From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] interconnect: qcom: sm8750: keep MC0 in the sleep set

On the AYN Odin 3, s2idle hangs, and a watchdog resets the device about
2.5 minutes later, whenever HLOS drops its MC0 vote to 0 in the sleep set
while the ADSP and CDSP are running. Until now the PCIe suspend OPP floor
hid it, because its memory-path vote happens to land on MC0.

Runtime bisection with the interconnect debugfs test client, floor
dropped and both DSPs running:
- a 1 kBps sleep-only vote llcc_mc -> ebi (MC0 only) resumes, also over
  120 s;
- a sleep-only vote that stops at qns_llcc (SH0 only) hangs;
- holding ACV at 0, AOSS prevent_ddr_collapse, a fixed DDR frequency and
  prevent_aoss_sleep all still hang.

Add keepalive_sleep, which extends a BCM's keepalive to one unit in the
sleep set, and set it for the SM8750 MC0. DDR never entered a low-power
state with the floor either, so this costs nothing over the floor.
---
--- a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpmh.h
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpmh.h
@@ -118,6 +118,7 @@
  * @enable_mask: optional mask to send as vote instead of vote_x/vote_y
  * @dirty: flag used to indicate whether the bcm needs to be committed
  * @keepalive: flag used to indicate whether a keepalive is required
+ * @keepalive_sleep: also keep a minimal vote in the sleep set
  * @aux_data: auxiliary data used when calculating threshold values and
  * communicating with RPMh
  * @list: used to link to other bcms when compiling lists for commit
@@ -135,6 +136,7 @@
 	u32 enable_mask;
 	bool dirty;
 	bool keepalive;
+	bool keepalive_sleep;
 	struct bcm_db aux_data;
 	struct list_head list;
 	struct list_head ws_list;
--- a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/bcm-voter.c
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/bcm-voter.c
@@ -122,6 +122,12 @@
 		bcm->vote_y[QCOM_ICC_BUCKET_AMC] = 1;
 		bcm->vote_y[QCOM_ICC_BUCKET_WAKE] = 1;
 	}
+
+	if (bcm->keepalive_sleep && bcm->vote_x[QCOM_ICC_BUCKET_SLEEP] == 0 &&
+	    bcm->vote_y[QCOM_ICC_BUCKET_SLEEP] == 0) {
+		bcm->vote_x[QCOM_ICC_BUCKET_SLEEP] = 1;
+		bcm->vote_y[QCOM_ICC_BUCKET_SLEEP] = 1;
+	}
 }
 
 static inline void tcs_cmd_gen(struct tcs_cmd *cmd, u64 vote_x, u64 vote_y,
--- a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/sm8750.c
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/sm8750.c
@@ -1084,9 +1084,14 @@
 	.nodes = { &qnm_lpass_lpinoc, &qns_lpass_aggnoc },
 };
 
+/*
+ * s2idle hangs, followed by a watchdog reset, if HLOS drops its MC0 vote to 0 in the
+ * sleep set while the DSPs are running. One unit is enough to avoid it.
+ */
 static struct qcom_icc_bcm bcm_mc0 = {
 	.name = "MC0",
 	.keepalive = true,
+	.keepalive_sleep = true,
 	.num_nodes = 1,
 	.nodes = { &ebi },
 };
